      1 docs/N105_CRYPTOGRAPHIC_VALIDATOR_IDENTITY.md:49:Vote acceptance now requires that votes from registered validators carry a valid signature. Unsigned or incorrectly signed votes are rejected with an error. Quorum counting is unchanged and uses the same active_validator_count logic, now operating over the registered validator identifiers. Proposer selection is unchanged and still uses round-robin selection over the registered identifiers. Equivocation detection remains functional, as it compares voter_id and block hashes. Signature validation adds an additional layer of evidence, because an equivocating validator must still sign both conflicting votes, making the proof of misbehavior cryptographically stronger. The performance impact is one Ed25519 verification per vote, which is a constant-time operation taking microseconds. There is no measurable impact on consensus throughput in test clusters.
